cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VocationOS in research, teaching, or applied work, please cite it."
title: "VocationOS: Evidence-grounded career decision safety"
abstract: >-
  A local-first daemon for career decisions such as applications, outreach,
  relocation, and licensing. It refuses to execute a consequential action
  unless every claim behind it traces to verified evidence and a human has
  signed an approval scoped to that exact action, and it refuses to mark the
  action complete without a trusted Ed25519 collector receipt. The refusal is
  logged either way. The controls are enforced in typed code and adversarial
  tests rather than in prompts or configuration flags.
